To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 4 other than $a_{42}=1$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}9 & -7 & 4 & 7 \\ -6 & -5 & -9 & 8 \\ -2 & 4 & 3 & -8 \\ -2 & 1 & 3 & 2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}+2C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 4 & 7 \\ -16 & -5 & -9 & 8 \\ 6 & 4 & 3 & -8 \\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 25 & 7 \\ -16 & -5 & 6 & 8 \\ 6 & 4 & -9 & -8 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{2}}\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 & 25 & 21 \\ -16 & -5 & 6 & 18 \\ 6 & 4 & -9 & -16 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}=B
$$

Therefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are

$C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{2}$ and $C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{2}$.
